diagnosis_text:
After a thorough investigation of router16, mswitch0, the three access switches, and every router in the OSPF domain, no fault was found. Router16 is fully operational: its bond0 interface (10.2.2.1/24, formed from eth0+eth1 in round-robin mode) is up and carrying traffic to mswitch0, and its eth2 (172.30.1.1/24) maintains a stable Full OSPF adjacency with router7 (~11 minutes uptime). mswitch0 is correctly running OSPF, advertising 172.16.10/20/30.0/24 as directly connected networks via its vlan10, vlan20, and vlan30 sub-interfaces. All three VLAN bridges on switches 1–3 are forwarding VLAN-tagged traffic correctly between the access PCs and mswitch0. End-to-end pings from router1, router7, router10, router11, and router17 to actual Campus 1 host IPs (172.16.10.5, 172.16.10.6, 172.16.20.9, 172.16.30.12) returned 0% packet loss, and Campus 1 PCs can reach all external subnets. The helpdesk ticket appears to describe a transient condition — most likely a brief period immediately after lab startup during which OSPF had not yet fully converged and the 172.16.x.x prefixes were not yet installed in the rest-of-network routing tables. The issue self-resolved within the normal OSPF convergence window. No corrective action is required.
